Summary: 

The word of this year is prioritization. November and December of 2024 were months of experimentation where I prioritized what I wanted against work, obligation, and cultural expectation. The consequence? I built confidence that I can have it all!! (Famous last words...)

Of course, this is all easier said than done. Once the throws of the year commence, the ability to choose will increase in difficulty. 

I have this application called Stoic App. I initially bought it to get quotes on my phone to compliment my reading of The Daily Stoic (by Ryan Holiday.) They're unrelated - Holiday and the app. I was surprised to find that there is a focus of the day prompt. What is your focus - select up to three. It then prompts you with questions related to that focus area. while the questions sometimes feel really superficial, I like this idea of creating an area of focus daily so that I can choose my own priority.

It being the first of the year, the question of resolutions come up. I am a proponent for resolutions, so here they are:
- Have a successful wedding
- Spend more time in nature
- Use my body in a broader range (e.g. dance)
- Spend time in my creativity

There are more, but these would be my top 4 for a fulfilling 2025.

What will ensure I stay on the path to my goals will be the following:
- Am I working for this tool or is the tool working for me?
- Am I doing this because I want to or because I think I should?

Here's to a wildly optimistic 2025. Cheers.